invariant: INV-26
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-trust-separation.sh
reason: the Makefile writes CH_AES_EXTERN_CONSTANT_TIME into every
  AES=extern object, so a SUITE=aesgcm AES=extern build compiles with
  the peripheral's timing asserted by a build file rather than by the
  firmware author who can answer for the part. ct.h's refusal then never
  fires for a build that makes no statement. lint-trust-separation's
  AES=extern suite rows ban the define in the object's defines.

--- old
AES_DEF := -DCH_AES_EXTERN
--- new
AES_DEF := -DCH_AES_EXTERN -DCH_AES_EXTERN_CONSTANT_TIME
